315
00:20:27,140 --> 00:20:29,390
No. No, that wouldn't be fair to me...

316
00:20:29,600 --> 00:20:31,390
...it wouldn't be fair to Alan, or to you.

317
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:33,680
Yeah, well, who wants fair?

318
00:20:33,890 --> 00:20:37,770
I mean, I just want things back, you know, the way they were.

319
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:43,900
- I'm sorry.     - Oh, she's sorry. I feel better.

320
00:20:45,660 --> 00:20:47,070
I just can't believe this.

321
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:51,950
I mean, with the holidays coming up. I wanted him to meet my family.

322
00:20:53,120 --> 00:20:56,170
I'll meet someone else. There'll be other Alans.

323
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,540
Yeah, right.

324
00:21:02,420 --> 00:21:05,970
- Are you guys gonna be okay?     - Hey, hey. We'll be fine.

325
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:08,800
We're just gonna need a little time.

326
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:11,310
I understand.

327
00:21:16,440 --> 00:21:17,850
Wow.

328
00:21:18,060 --> 00:21:21,980
- I'm really sorry.     - Yeah. I mean, I'm sorry too.

329
00:21:22,610 --> 00:21:24,780
But I gotta tell you, I'm a little relieved.

330
00:21:24,990 --> 00:21:26,860
- Relieved?     - Yeah, well...

331
00:21:27,070 --> 00:21:29,410
...I mean, I had a great time with you.

332
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,830
I just can't stand your friends.

333
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:42,380
Remember when we went to Central Park and rented boats?

334
00:21:44,420 --> 00:21:46,170
That was fun.

335
00:21:46,720 --> 00:21:50,260
Yeah. He could row like a Viking.

336
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:57,100
- Hi.     - Hi.

337
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:00,940
So how'd it go?

338
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:04,940
- You know.     - Did he mention us?

339
